{% extends 'admin/_main/layout.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}New credit note | Admin{% endblock %}

{#
    The create page with NOBODY in scope — reached from the sidebar's Create Credit Note, and from
    the grid's New credit note button when the grid is not scoped to one company.

    Before this, admin_credit_memo_new answered that case by flashing "open one from an invoice, or
    from a company" and redirecting to the grid, so the only ways to raise a note were from an
    invoice, from an RMA, or from a company-scoped grid. #586 is explicit that a standalone credit —
    goodwill, a pricing correction, credit raised before anyone decides which invoice it lands
    against — is a first-class case, and a first-class case needs a door.

    The shape is OrderController::create()'s, deliberately: a plain <select> of companies posted
    back to the SAME route, which recognises a pick (no draft fields on it) and redirects to
    `?company=`, re-entering the editor knowing who the note is for. Two requests rather than one
    because the customer decides the addresses, the company snapshot and the region the draft is
    built from — settled before the draft exists, not read off the POST that creates it.

    It lives in its own template rather than as an `{% if not company %}` arm inside
    edit.html.twig — which is how the order form does it — because edit.html.twig is the shared
    new/edit draft editor and every line of it assumes a company. The pattern that matters is the
    behaviour, and it is the same one; what differs is that the branch is not wrapped around 140
    lines that can never render in this state.

    No JavaScript anywhere in it: a real <form>, a real <select>, a real submit.
#}
{% block admin_body %}
    <section class="panel compact-panel">
        <div class="panel-title-row">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Credit note</p>
                <h1>New credit note</h1>
            </div>
            <div class="panel-actions">
                <a class="button back-button" href="{{ path('admin_credit_memo_index') }}">Back</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <form method="post" action="{{ path('admin_credit_memo_new') }}" id="credit-memo-company-form">
        {{ csrf_field() }}

        <section class="form-card">
            {% if creditMemoError %}
                {# Printed here as well as in the flash bag: the flash markup is hidden until
                   JavaScript lifts it out, and this screen has to read correctly without any. #}
                <p class="field-error">{{ creditMemoError }}</p>
            {% endif %}
            <div class="form-grid">
                <label class="full-width" for="company_id">
                    Customer <span class="req">*</span>
                    <select id="company_id" name="company_id" required>
                        <option value=""></option>
                        {% for row in companies %}
                            <option value="{{ row.id }}">{{ row.name }}{% if row.email %} - {{ row.email }}{% endif %}</option>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </select>
                    {% if companies is empty %}
                        <small>No customers exist yet. <a href="{{ path('admin_company_create') }}">Add one</a> before raising a credit note.</small>
                    {% endif %}
                </label>

                <div class="form-actions">
                    <button class="button primary" type="submit">Next</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </form>
{% endblock %}
